{"title":"Combined feed","url":"https://Vinnl.github.io/feeds/all.xml","elements":[{"title":"Guy Standing (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that this photograph <i>(pictured)</i> of British economist <b><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guy_Standing_(economist)\" title=\"Guy Standing (economist)\">Guy Standing</a></b> caused a Wikipedia edit war?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guy_Standing_(economist)","retrieved":1788033345715},{"title":"Ode to Massachusetts (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that a man spent four years trying to make his song \"<b><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ode_to_Massachusetts\" title=\"Ode to Massachusetts\">Ode to Massachusetts</a></b>\" the official state ode?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ode_to_Massachusetts","retrieved":1788033345716},{"title":"Ildibad (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that one historian described the Gothic king <b><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ildibad\" title=\"Ildibad\">Ildibad</a></b> being struck so suddenly by one of his bodyguards that he was still holding the food he was eating when his head fell to the ground?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ildibad","retrieved":1788033345719},{"title":"omnisexuality (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that some people think that <b><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Omnisexuality\" title=\"Omnisexuality\">omnisexuality</a></b> is distinct from pansexuality?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Omnisexuality","retrieved":1788033345719},{"title":"Lea VanderVelde (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that <b><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lea_VanderVelde\" title=\"Lea VanderVelde\">Lea VanderVelde</a></b> had co-nominated the 2014 Nobel Peace Prize winner nine times before he won?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lea_VanderVelde","retrieved":1788033345723},{"title":"a conspiracy (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Communist_Party_of_Ukraine_(Soviet_Union)\" title=\"Communist Party of Ukraine (Soviet Union)\">Communist Party of Ukraine</a> was allowed to continue their activities after being involved in <b><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polonsky_conspiracy\" title=\"Polonsky conspiracy\">a conspiracy</a></b> to assassinate <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nestor_Makhno\" title=\"Nestor Makhno\">Nestor Makhno</a>?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polonsky_conspiracy","retrieved":1788033345724},{"title":"Kuzushiro (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that as a university student and manga assistant, <b><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kuzushiro\" title=\"Kuzushiro\">Kuzushiro</a></b> said she sometimes stayed overnight at her workplace while helping produce a weekly series?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kuzushiro","retrieved":1788033345725},{"title":"7 Dogs (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that <i><b><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/7_Dogs\" title=\"7 Dogs\">7 Dogs</a></b></i> broke two film-explosion world records previously held by two <i>James Bond</i> films?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/7_Dogs","retrieved":1788033345725},{"title":"a Swiss pig castrator (Wikipedia — did you know?)","contents":"... that one of the first caesarean sections in which both the mother and the infant survived may have been performed by <b><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacob_Nufer\" title=\"Jacob Nufer\">a Swiss pig castrator</a></b> on his own wife?","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacob_Nufer","retrieved":1788033345728},{"title":"Destination of the Month (Wikivoyage recommendations)","contents":"<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt8\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwIQ\" data-m